From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: keep a BO's CPU mapping while it is in the BO cache

panfrost_bo_unreference() unmapped every BO before putting it in the
cache, so each reuse of a cached BO paid an mmap, the page faults of
touching it again and, at its next release, a munmap. Batch pool slabs
are released and fetched again every frame: Flycast (Dead or Alive 2) on
Mali-G31 spent ~11 % of its rendering thread in mmap, munmap and the
faults. The mapping now stays until the BO is freed (cache eviction,
including a BO the kernel purged while evictable: making it unevictable
fails and it is freed).

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_bo.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_bo.c
@@ -121,6 +121,8 @@
    return NULL;
 }
 
+static void panfrost_bo_munmap(struct panfrost_bo *bo);
+
 static void
 panfrost_bo_free(struct panfrost_bo *bo)
 {
@@ -128,6 +130,9 @@
    struct pan_kmod_vm *vm = bo->dev->kmod.vm;
    uint64_t gpu_va = bo->ptr.gpu;
 
+   /* A cached BO keeps its CPU mapping until it is freed. */
+   panfrost_bo_munmap(bo);
+
    /* BO will be freed with the sparse array, but zero to indicate free */
    memset(bo, 0, sizeof(*bo));
 
@@ -458,9 +463,11 @@
     * lock, let's make sure it's still not referenced before freeing it.
     */
    if (p_atomic_read(&bo->refcnt) == 0) {
-      /* When the reference count goes to zero, we need to cleanup */
-      panfrost_bo_munmap(bo);
-
+      /* When the reference count goes to zero, we need to cleanup. The
+       * CPU mapping stays while the BO is in the cache (it is unmapped
+       * when the BO is freed, also when the kernel purged it meanwhile):
+       * unmapping on every release cost an mmap, page faults and a munmap
+       * at each reuse, e.g. every batch pool slab of every frame. */
       if (dev->debug & (PAN_DBG_TRACE | PAN_DBG_SYNC))
          pandecode_inject_free(dev->decode_ctx, bo->ptr.gpu,
                                panfrost_bo_size(bo));
